# Try the API by hand: start it with "dotnet run --project src/PBRMS.Api",
# then click "Send Request" above each block (VS Code needs the REST Client extension;
# Visual Studio and Rider support .http files out of the box).

@api = http://localhost:5188

### Is the API up, and can it reach the database?
GET {{api}}/health

### Sign in as a sample user (Development only). Other emails are in src/PBRMS.Data/DevSeed.cs.
# @name login
POST {{api}}/auth/dev-login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "supervisor@pbrms.test" }

### Who am I? Uses the token from the sign-in above.
GET {{api}}/me
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.token}}
